Additional implementation details:
- Built-in skills now tell the model to call the native helper functions through the approved PowerShell tool for clipboard, window enumeration, UIA, settings launch, and system summary.
- The helper recognizes when it is executing inside an already-approved `run_powershell` call, avoiding a second redundant confirmation. Direct CLI modifications still prompt in ASK mode; headless ASK fails closed.
- Native Win32 helper initialization is lazy and only occurs for clipboard/window commands.
- Headless request handling does not poll console keys or render the interactive spinner. JSON mode returns one structured response object on success and a structured error on request failure.
- Added interactive `.skills` and `.skill <name>` commands; user-authored skill files are read from `$HOME\.gemma\skills\`.

